WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.580
Command and control means unauthorized communication that allows an affected asset,

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.370
account, workload, or service to receive direction or send

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.810
status outside normal trust boundaries.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.660
Defenders should treat this stage as a question about communication evidence,

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.920
not as a lesson in setup or evasion.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.880
Useful signals may appear in DNS logs, proxy logs, firewall records, endpoint telemetry,

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.310
cloud network flow records,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.455
identity events, or SaaS activity logs.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.070
The details vary by environment.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.835
A workstation, a container workload, a cloud function,

00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:31.360
and a compromised account may all create different communication patterns.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.225
Defensive controls include egress filtering, destination allowlists, segmentation,

00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:38.960
proxy inspection, anomaly detection, and rapid containment paths.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.770
Analysts should ask what communicated, where it communicated, how often,

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.160
through which control point,

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.430
and whether that behavior matches expected business activity.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.120
Containment decisions should be evidence based.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.330
Isolating a host, disabling a credential, blocking a destination,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.370
or segmenting a workload can reduce risk,

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.020
but those actions should be recorded and coordinated.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.780
The value of this stage is to make outbound visibility and containment planning part of

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.280
normal defensive readiness.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.320
This stage is a reminder that outbound visibility matters as much as inbound defense.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.090
If the organization cannot explain which systems can reach which destinations,

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.560
containment becomes slower and less precise.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.800
Well-governed egress makes unusual communication easier to notice and easier to limit.
